# Hot Wire, by GLM 5.3 and SZ. An original peak-time electro-house track for the Techno style, in
# the spirit of the filtered-riff club 12-inches: one catchy, instantly hummable riff carries the
# whole song - an octave leap up on beat 1, a 7-5-3 cascade down through the chord on beat 2, and a
# rising pickup back to the hook - on the acid lead, doubled in driven radio grit (inst=radio-lead)
# in the full sections, over a 909 kit and a sub locked to the kick. Brighter and more playful than
# the other Techno originals: the riff bounces over an Am - F - C - G loop, off-beat stab skanks and
# a dark pad fill the middle, and a chopped wordless vocal (inst=vox-lead) echoes the riff's cascade
# in the drops and sings over the second breakdown.
#
# The chord loop is Am - F - C - G, one chord a bar, for all 144 bars. The riff is one rhythmic
# template per chord: root and octave on beats 1 and 1.5, a 7-5-3 cascade landing on the third on
# beat 2, a written echo of the octave (in the breakdowns) and a rising 5-7 pickup on beat 3, and
# the octave and root again on beat 4. Every 8th bar the G bar climbs D-F-G-A-B-D instead.
# chords: Am F C G
#
# Form 1-16: DJ intro - kick, then hats, then the sub
# Form 17-32: the riff teased and filtered in (a velocity ramp), the pad under it
# Form 33-48: first groove - riff and its grit double, off-beat stabs, claps, open hats
# Form 49-56: breakdown 1 - the kick drops, the pad and riff carry, with written echoes
# Form 57-64: build 1 - snare roll quarters into eighths into sixteenths, an acid riser climbing
# Form 65-80: drop 1 - everything, the vocal echoing the cascade in the second half
# Form 81-88: breakdown 2 - the kick drops again, the vocal sings over the pad and riff
# Form 89-96: build 2 - the roll starts faster, the riser an octave up
# Form 97-128: final drop - 16th hats, a rolling sub with octave pops, vocal chops, then the riff
#              doubled an octave up on the square stab for the last 16 bars
# Form 129-144: outro - drums, sub and stabs, then stripped to the kick for the mixer
#
# Human feel: the kick and riff stay on the grid (a sequencer), while the off-beat hats swing a
# few ticks late in the grooves, the claps drag +11 to +16, the stabs land +14 to +22, and every
# hat, clap and stab has an uneven velocity.
title: Hot Wire
composer: GLM 5.3 & SZ
about: Peak-time electro house at 128 in A minor: one catchy octave-leaping riff on the acid lead, doubled in driven grit, over a pumping sub and a 909, with chopped vocals echoing the drops.
year: 2026
source: original
category: originals
style: techno
key: A minor
tempo: 128
time: 4/4

